# Livestock Real-Time Tracking (Redis)
# Tracking animal movements via GPS/RFID collars for grazing management.

# 1. Update Animal Locations (Geo)
# GEOADD key lon lat member
GEOADD ranch:herd:cattle -98.5795 29.4241 "TAG-001"
GEOADD ranch:herd:cattle -98.5790 29.4245 "TAG-002"

# 2. Check for Strays (Geofence)
# Defined Safe Zone Center: -98.58, 29.42
# Find all animals OUTSIDE the 1km radius (Logic handled by app comparing radius)
# Here we find animals INSIDE:
GEORADIUS ranch:herd:cattle -98.58 29.42 1 km WITHDIST

# 3. Store Real-Time Vitals (Hash)
# Smart collar data: Body Temp, Activity Level (Steps)
HSET animal:vitals:TAG-001 temp_c 38.5 activity_level "HIGH" heart_rate 60
HSET animal:vitals:TAG-002 temp_c 39.1 activity_level "LOW" heart_rate 55

# 4. Estrus Detection Alert (Pub/Sub)
# High activity + specific temp change might indicate estrus (breeding window).
PUBLISH ranch:alerts "POSSIBLE_ESTRUS: TAG-001 Activity Spike Detected"
